This assert statement means that, in the array list (arrList), it checks if the last index of a number 'x', is equal to or higher than the index of that 'x'. If the condition is not satisfied, the method fails and a test case with this assert will fail. 'IndexOf(x)' retrieves the index of the first occurrence of 'x' in Array List and 'LastIndexOf(x)' retrieves the index of the last occurrence of 'x' in the Array List. If their relationship is 'LastIndexOf(x) >= IndexOf(x)', it allows at least one instance of element 'x' to be in the array list. If a collection contains multiple instances of 'x' the 'IndexOf(x)' gives index of first 'x' and 'LastIndexOf(x)' gives the last 'x', Hence, 'Last index is Greater than or equal to first index' in the array.--------------------
